## Models carried

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| what-if-list | New in kindergarten (th-k-imagine, model_out) | Unit 1: the picture card of "what if" ideas for the imagined place (what if the floor is a river, what if we are tiny) | Unit 5 (what a character might choose, th-g1-imagine), unit 9 (new details and lines, th-g2-imagine) |
| group-agreements | New in kindergarten (th-k-show, model_out) | Unit 1: the picture card of the class's drama agreements (take turns, add on, freeze on the signal, join when ready) | Unit 5 (group decisions, th-g1-show), unit 9 (deciding how the story goes on, th-g2-show); shown in every set-up as review |
| warm-up-routine | New in kindergarten (th-k-actor, model_out) | Unit 2: the children's voice and sound warm-up (hum, big and small sounds, a character's voice). Unit 1 opens with the teacher's two-minute "ready body" set-up only, not this routine | Unit 6 (face, body and gesture added, th-g1-actor), unit 10 (body, mind and voice together, th-g2-actor); every later day's warm-up as review |
| audience-journal | New in kindergarten (th-k-notice, model_out) | Unit 2: the folder of audience cards (circle a face, draw the part you liked) | Unit 6 (choices remembered and compared, th-g1-notice), unit 10 (decision moments, th-g2-notice); each later unit's showing day as review |
| prop-sketch | New in kindergarten (th-k-design, model_out) | Unit 3: a drawing of the puppet or prop before it is made, with the teacher's label | Unit 7 (costume and prop planned, th-g1-design), unit 11 (a simple set planned, th-g2-design) |
| two-ties | New in kindergarten (th-k-world, model_out) | Unit 3: the card with two ties: how a character is like me, and a skill from another subject used in the play | Unit 7 (feelings tied to my life, th-g1-world), unit 11 (experiences related, know-how chosen, th-g2-world) |
| story-map | New in kindergarten (th-k-story, model_out) | Unit 4: the picture map of who and where in a tale | Unit 8 (what a character does and why, th-g1-story), unit 12 (causes and results across versions, th-g2-story) |

All seven go on to grade 3 (th-g3 rows' model_in); grade 3 adds rehearsal-log, character-map and criteria-card.

