## Seams

### Picked up from the course before

Kindergarten opens the band and the subject: there is no course before and no pre-kindergarten course. The seven
kindergarten threads that start here with no earlier row are th-k-imagine, th-k-show, th-k-actor, th-k-design,
th-k-story, th-k-world and th-k-notice (their `assumes` cells are empty); each is first used in the unit named in the
table below.

### Inside the band: year to year

Each row of years 1 and 2 assumes the year before's row in its thread (one grade back), so it opens as a retrieval
task inside day 2 of its unit.

| Thread | Year K row (unit, course days) | Year 1 row that picks it up (unit) | Year 2 row that picks it up (unit) | What changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Imagining | th-k-imagine (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | th-g1-imagine (unit 5): a character's choice suggested, a plot built in order | th-g2-imagine (unit 9) retrieves th-g1-imagine (unit 5, days 65 to 80): new details, voice and sound to tell the tale, dialogue made up | Enter a place with help, then choices and a plot in order, then details and dialogue |
| Playing together | th-k-show (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | th-g1-show (unit 5): group decisions and a changed plot | th-g2-show (unit 9) retrieves th-g1-show (unit 5, days 65 to 80): lines changed and a scene shared with the class | Join and add, then decide and change, then work up and share a scene |
| The actor's tools | th-k-actor (unit 2, days 19 to 36) | th-g1-actor (unit 6): face, body, gesture and voice show traits and feelings | th-g2-actor (unit 10) retrieves th-g1-actor (unit 6, days 81 to 102): small differences in one character, adjusted as you go | Voice and sound, then the whole body, then fine adjustment |
| Watching and reacting | th-k-notice (unit 2, days 19 to 36) | th-g1-notice (unit 6): choices remembered, self compared with a character | th-g2-notice (unit 10) retrieves th-g1-notice (unit 6, days 81 to 102): decision moments spotted, others compared with a character | How I feel, then what I remember and how I compare, then how others decide and feel |
| Making for a drama | th-k-design (unit 3, days 39 to 52) | th-g1-design (unit 7): costume and prop planned, tech named, one object as many things | th-g2-design (unit 11) retrieves th-g1-design (unit 7, days 105 to 116): a set planned, an effect tried, a place shown by a prop | Make with help, then plan and name, then plan a set and try effects |
| Ties to me and to other subjects | th-k-world (unit 3, days 39 to 52) | th-g1-world (unit 7): a character's feeling tied to the child's life, another subject brought in | th-g2-world (unit 11) retrieves th-g1-world (unit 7, days 105 to 116): experiences related, the fitting know-how chosen | Like me, then feels like me, then lived like me, and the child chooses the outside skill |
| Story | th-k-story (unit 4, days 55 to 64) | th-g1-story (unit 8): actions and their causes, community stories, a scene from fiction | th-g2-story (unit 12) retrieves th-g1-story (unit 8, days 119 to 128): causes and results, stories from several cultures, a scene from nonfiction | Who and where, then why, then what follows and across cultures |

### Handed on to Theater, grades 3 to 5

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (grade 3) | What grade 3 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| th-g2-imagine | 9 | th-g3-imagine | Whole characters and settings invented through improvisation, and a method for finding ideas |
