ound words; review of kindergarten, then letters and sounds re-taught with short a, i and u and the digraphs th, ch and sh, and qu, with plural -s first met (Skills Block cycles 1 to 4); grade 1 irregular words by mapping; printing every letter and spelling taught patterns; fluency in decodable and short grade 1 texts: reading on-level text with purpose, aloud with accuracy, rate and expression on rereading, and using context to confirm or self-correct a word already decoded (RF.1.4a to c). Continued all year: e1-phonemes, e1-irregular-words, e1-spell-and-print and e1-fluency. e1-short-vowels continues in unit 2 (short o and e, wh and -ck, doubled finals, clusters, -ng and -nk, cycles 5 to 11). | The base text's module 1, six weeks, built for launching routines in reading, talk and writing. The placement screen and short-vowel review come first because every pattern after rests on them. The topic is concrete and every child knows someone who works with tools; the informative piece uses the main-idea-details model carried from kindergarten and starts the paragraph-frame. | Candidate: the base text's module 1 unit assessments, adapted (key details and pictures in a text about tools; describing a character; the informative tool piece and the designed tool) and the Skills Block cycle 1 to 4 checks, on short a, i and u and th, ch, sh only; checked in the unit plan. | Work at home differs: children talk about workers they have met or read about, never about whether a parent has a job. Tool safety: real tools are shown by the teacher, never handled with blades. Names and photographs on the class wall stay in the room. |
