84: - **Day kinds.** As docs/GLOSSARY.md ("teaching day") and APPROACH "Kinds of day". Understanding: a technique shown in
85:   named steps with the step card (a freeze, a walk, a cross, a cue), or a work watched, heard or described and
86:   studied with the unit's words (the artistic process "responding" is taught here, never on a respond day).
87:   Fluency: the warm-up routine and a scene beat run several times with feedback (a mirror exercise, a walk changed
88:   three ways, a line said with three hidden thoughts); in grades 3 to 5 it is the five-minute warm-up and two fluency
89:   days a unit. Application: improvising, rehearsing, sketching and making with some choice of role, line, job or
90:   design; the second rehearsal day holds the unit's one critique (describe, ask, suggest), and the next day's
91:   revision is application too. Check: the showing day and the written day of the unit's evidence line. Respond: a
